1
00:02:23,225 --> 00:02:29,225
For a bunch of funny friends trying to break into show
business... it's a jungle out there!

2
00:04:46,451 --> 00:04:52,451
Cats Don't Dance is a animation, comedy, family film directed by Mark Dindal.

3
00:07:09,677 --> 00:07:15,677
An ambitious singing and dancing cat in 1939 Hollywood overcomes several
obstacles to fulfill his dream of becoming a movie star.

4
00:09:32,903 --> 00:09:38,903
Danny (voice), played by Scott Bakula.

5
00:11:56,129 --> 00:12:02,129
Sawyer (voice), played by Jasmine Guy.

6
00:14:19,354 --> 00:14:25,354
Sawyer (singing voice), played by Natalie Cole.

7
00:16:42,580 --> 00:16:48,580
Darla Dimple (voice), played by Ashley Peldon.

8
00:19:05,806 --> 00:19:11,806
Darla Dimple (singing voice), played by Lindsay Ridgeway.

9
00:21:29,032 --> 00:21:35,032
Farley Wink (voice), played by Frank Welker.

10
00:23:52,258 --> 00:23:58,258
Cats Don't Dance is a 1997 American animated musical
comedy film directed by Mark Dindal.

11
00:26:15,483 --> 00:26:21,483
The film features the voices of Scott Bakula, Jasmine Guy, Matthew Herried, Ashley Peldon, John Rhys-Davies, Kathy Najimy, Don
Knotts, Hal Holbrook, Betty Lou Gerson (in her final film role), René Auberjonois, Mark Dindal, and George Kennedy.

12
00:28:38,709 --> 00:28:44,709
In 1993, Cats Don't Dance originated as a proposed film
collaboration between Michael Jackson and David Kirschner.

13
00:31:01,935 --> 00:31:07,935
It was announced as a live-action/animated film project with Jackson
attached to star, and consult on the music and choreography.

14
00:33:25,161 --> 00:33:31,161
However, by 1994, Jackson dropped out of the project.

15
00:35:48,387 --> 00:35:54,387
The project was reverted to Turner Feature Animation, and reconceived into a
fully animated film that homaged classic Hollywood musical films.

16
00:38:11,612 --> 00:38:17,612
Mark Dindal was hired as the director.

17
00:40:34,838 --> 00:40:40,838
The film's musical numbers were written by Randy Newman.

18
00:42:58,064 --> 00:43:04,064
Gene Kelly consulted with the animators on the
choreography before his death in 1996.

19
00:45:21,290 --> 00:45:27,290
The film was Kelly's final film project and is dedicated to his memory.

20
00:47:44,516 --> 00:47:50,516
In 1996, Turner Broadcasting System was merged with Time Warner, and as a result, Cats Don't
Dance was the only fully animated feature produced by Turner Feature Animation.

21
00:50:07,741 --> 00:50:13,741
Cats Don't Dance was released in the United States and
Canada on March 26, 1997, by Warner Bros.

22
00:52:30,967 --> 00:52:36,967
under its Family Entertainment label.

23
00:54:54,193 --> 00:55:00,193
The film received generally positive reviews from critics.

24
00:57:17,419 --> 00:57:23,419
However, it was a box-office failure, grossing $3.5
million in the United States and Canada.

25
00:59:40,645 --> 00:59:46,645
The film's producer David Kirschner blamed Warner Bros.

26
01:02:03,870 --> 01:02:09,870
for a failed marketing campaign and lack of promotional tie-ins.

27
01:04:27,096 --> 01:04:33,096
Cats Don't Dance won two Annie Awards, one for Best Animated Feature
and the other for Best Music in a Feature Production.

28
01:06:50,322 --> 01:06:56,322
It was the first non-Disney animated film to win in either category.

29
01:09:13,548 --> 01:09:19,548
The film explores themes of dance, villain,
musical, anthropomorphism, hollywood.

30
01:11:36,774 --> 01:11:42,774
The tone is lighthearted.
